        <!-- post -->
        <div id="post-720" class="post-720 post type-post status-publish format-standard hentry category-net">

          <div class="post-header">
           <h3 class="post-title"><a href="http://blog.cromwellhaus.com/2008/07/why-plain-old-linq-is-so-powerful/" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link: Why Plain Old LINQ is so powerful">Why Plain Old LINQ is so powerful</a></h3>
           <p class="post-date">
            <span class="month">Jul</span>
            <span class="day">31</span>
           </p>
           <p class="post-author">
            <span class="info">Posted by <a href="http://blog.cromwellhaus.com/author/cromwellryan/" title="Posts by cromwellryan ">cromwellryan</a> in <a href="http://blog.cromwellhaus.com/category/net/" title="View all posts in .Net" rel="category tag">.Net</a> | <a href="http://blog.cromwellhaus.com/2008/07/why-plain-old-linq-is-so-powerful/#comments" class="comments"  title="Comment on Why Plain Old LINQ is so powerful"><span class="dsq-postid" rel="720 /blogs/ryanc/archive/2008/07/31/why-plain-old-linq-is-so-powerful.aspx">1 Comment</span></a>              </span>
           </p>
          </div>

          <div class="post-content clearfix">
          <p>Ian Griffiths posted a great example of how powerful and cool LINQ is when used in everyday code (it&#8217;s not all about databases people). If you haven&#8217;t started to learn how to incorporate this awesome toolset into your daily coding life, you&#8217;re killing yourself.&nbsp; No excuses.</p>

                    </div>
        </div>
        <!-- /post -->
        
        <!-- post -->
        <div id="post-719" class="post-719 post type-post status-publish format-standard hentry category-net">

          <div class="post-header">
           <h3 class="post-title"><a href="http://blog.cromwellhaus.com/2008/07/roadblock-to-mocking-unit-tests/" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link: Roadblock to Mocking Unit Tests">Roadblock to Mocking Unit Tests</a></h3>
           <p class="post-date">
            <span class="month">Jul</span>
            <span class="day">15</span>
           </p>
           <p class="post-author">
            <span class="info">Posted by <a href="http://blog.cromwellhaus.com/author/cromwellryan/" title="Posts by cromwellryan ">cromwellryan</a> in <a href="http://blog.cromwellhaus.com/category/net/" title="View all posts in .Net" rel="category tag">.Net</a> | <a href="http://blog.cromwellhaus.com/2008/07/roadblock-to-mocking-unit-tests/#comments" class="comments"  title="Comment on Roadblock to Mocking Unit Tests"><span class="dsq-postid" rel="719 /blogs/ryanc/archive/2008/07/15/roadblock-to-mocking-unit-tests.aspx">14 Comments</span></a>              </span>
           </p>
          </div>

          <div class="post-content clearfix">
          <p>I&#8217;ve been a faithful unit tester for a few years now.&nbsp; I may not do everything by the book (I think end-to-end unit tests are helpful), but I do get good coverage most of the time.&nbsp; That said, I&#8217;ve found myself unable to use any of the Mock frameworks out there, because I don&#8217;t use [...]</p>

                    </div>
        </div>
